Reject HTTP provider downloads that exceed size-limit.

A truncated body can still parse and overwrite the working cache.
Read one byte past the limit and reject oversized responses before
hashing or parsing them. An exact fit is accepted, and nonpositive
limits continue to allow downloads of any size.

